recent.desc:
In January 1066 King Edward the Confessor died without a son, and three men fought for his crown:
- Harold Godwinson, Earl of Wessex and the most powerful man in England, who was crowned the next day;
- Duke William of Normandy, who said Edward had promised the throne to him;
- King Harald Hardrada of Norway.

In September Hardrada invaded the north. Harold marched up from London and defeated him
